.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt UUCP 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm uucp
.Nd copy files or queue them for a configured uucp peer
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl cCdfjmrR
.Op Fl g Ar grade
.Op Fl n Ar user
.Op Fl x Ar debug
.Ar source ...
.Ar destination
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility copies local files or queues a bounded copy/fetch job for a configured peer.
A local destination is copied immediately.
A destination of the form
.Ql system!path
is queued under
.Pa /var/spool/uucp
because this image has no transport.
.Pp
A source may also use
.Ql system!path
to queue a fetch to a local destination.
Remote-to-remote copies are rejected.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c
Accept the spool-copy compatibility flag. The queue always embeds the payload.
.It Fl C
Same as
.Fl c .
.It Fl d
Create missing local destination directories.
.It Fl f
Do not create local destination directories (the default).
.It Fl j
Print each queued job id.
.It Fl m
Accept the mail-completion flag; no mail transport exists.
.It Fl r
Accept the no-start flag; jobs are always queued.
.It Fl R
Accept the restart flag; jobs are always queued.
.It Fl g Ar grade
Set the one-byte job grade (default
.Ql n ) .
.It Fl n Ar user
Set the requesting user name.
.It Fl x Ar debug
Parse and ignore a debug level.
.El
.Pp
A destination with multiple local sources must already be a directory.
The default peer and spool settings come from
.Pa /etc/uucp/config ;
see
.Xr uustat 1
and
.Xr uux 1 .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /var/spool/uucp -compact
.It Pa /etc/uucp/config
Peer and spool configuration.
.It Pa /var/spool/uucp/queue
Queued job records.
.It Pa /var/spool/uucp/seq
Next queue sequence number.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A file, peer or queue error exits with status 1; a usage error exits with status 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr uustat 1 ,
.Xr uux 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD implements a bounded POSIX uucp file-transfer subset. No transport, modem or remote
execution is claimed; the local queue is the durable surface.
.Sh LIMITATIONS
Remote-to-remote copies, mail notification, debug transcripts and actual peer transmission are
not implemented.
